  "liner": {
   "body_md": "This audience recording captures Mountain Goats performing at Crossing Borders in Amsterdam on October 9, 1999 [1]. It is the only archived recording of this specific show, which is the 25th of 467 in the archive's collection for the performer [3]. The setlist includes thirteen songs, beginning with a cover of The Extra Glenns' \"Somebody Else's Parking Lot in Santa Cruz,\" a track that is the only archived performance of its kind [1]. Other highlights include \"Prana Ferox,\" \"West Country Dream,\" and \"Standard Bitter Love Song #1,\" the latter being the first in the archive [1]. The performance also features covers of Steely Dan's \"Doctor Wu\" and Neutral Milk Hotel's \"Two-Headed Boy,\" the latter being the only archived performance of that song [1]. A 2016 review of this specific recording by a listener describes it as both the best and worst they have heard from the band [2]. The reviewer specifically praised the cover of \"Two-Headed Boy\" as the best rendition of that Neutral Milk Hotel song, despite the performer messing up the lyrics [2]. They also noted that classics like \"Going to Georgia,\" \"Prana Ferox,\" and \"Standard Bitter Love Song\" were played at their best [2]. The recording is rated 5 out of 5 by one listener [1].",
